## Vendor-tarball realization of the ``openclaw`` interface: the npm registry
## tarball plus a per-platform dependency closure.
##
## ## Provenance, in words
##
## OpenClaw is source-available (MIT; evidence in the interface header:
## the tarball's ``LICENSE`` equals
## https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/v2026.11.5/LICENSE).
## This realization is NOT a from-source build. It repacks the artifact
## upstream publishes to npm, which is a compiled ``dist/`` (the pnpm
## workspace is not built here), and must not be presented as equivalent
## provenance. A from-source realization is not expressible: the catalog's
## ``packages/source/`` tier has no recipe form, and the build is a pnpm
## monorepo build with patches (``pnpm-workspace.yaml``, ``patches/``).
##
## ## Version and channel
##
## 2026.11.5, npm dist-tag ``latest`` (also ``beta``) on 2026-11-17;
## ``extended-stable`` is 2026.9.37. The consuming workspace's current
## source build is 2026.9.5, which is still on the registry but is not
## the current release; the catalog pins the current one. Upstream's GitHub
## release for the same tag also carries Linux AppImage/deb desktop
## packages; those are the desktop application, not this CLI, and are not
## used.
##
## ## The root archive
##
## ``https://registry.npmjs.org/openclaw/-/openclaw-2026.11.5.tgz``, 117,357,557
## bytes, 19,517 files, 305 MB unpacked, ``strip-components 1`` (everything
## sits under ``package/``). ``bin`` is ``openclaw`` -> ``openclaw.mjs``,
## which is ``executablePath`` with ``launcher = "node"`` and
## ``executableAlias = "openclaw"``, the pattern the other npm agents use.
##
## The digest is SELF-COMPUTED, because npm publishes only a sha512
## ``integrity`` and the tarball record verifies sha256: downloaded on
## 2026-11-17 and hashed with sha256sum. The sha512 integrity npm publishes
## (``sha512-mqPlsGLOe8NS85...``) was recomputed over the same bytes and
## matches, which is what ties the sha256 to upstream's own statement.
##
## Three packages (``@homebridge/ciao``, ``chrome-devtools-mcp``,
## ``playwright-core``) are ``bundleDependencies`` and ship inside the root
## tarball's own ``node_modules``; they are not in the closure.
##
## ## The closure: why it exists, and what it is not
##
## The package declares 77 dependencies and 84 optional ones, among them
## native add-ons chosen per platform (esbuild, sqlite-vec, node-pty,
## resvg, fs-safe, proc-safe, cua-driver). It does not run without them.
## ``closures/openclaw-<npm os>-<npm cpu>.manifest`` is generated: every
## entry is the ``resolved`` URL npm recorded for the closure npm itself
## computed (``npm install openclaw@2026.11.5 --package-lock-only`` with
## npm 10.9.3), with the sha256 of the archive that URL serves, written by
## ``tools/npm_closure_manifest.nim --build-closure``. 367 entries for the
## linux slices, 363 for macos and windows x86_64, 362 for windows arm64.
##
## Two deviations from the amp recipe's route, both forced:
##
## * ``tools/npm_closure_manifest.nim --root=openclaw`` cannot be used. It
##   resolves every dependency at the top-level ``node_modules/<name>`` and
##   stops with "not in the lock file: playwright-core" on a root that has
##   ``bundleDependencies``; and it has no notion of NESTED entries, of
##   which this lock has 23 (``node_modules/express/node_modules/content-type``
##   and others) where a dependency needs a different version than the one
##   hoisted. A flat closure would have placed the wrong version silently.
##   The ``--build-closure`` mode keeps the nested paths, so it was used on
##   the lock reduced, per platform, to the entries npm would install there
##   (same ``os``/``cpu`` rule as the tool's ``admits``; the root's own
##   entry removed). The reduced lock is a scratch file named in each
##   manifest's header; it is not committed.
## * The tool does not filter on ``libc``, so the linux slices carry both the
##   ``-gnu`` and ``-musl`` builds of each native add-on. Only size is
##   affected: the loader picks the one that fits.
##
## Verified on linux x86_64 only (2026-11-17): the root tarball plus the
## linux-x64 manifest, each archive checked against its manifest sha256 and
## unpacked at its path, gave a prefix in which
## ``node openclaw.mjs --version`` printed ``OpenClaw 2026.11.5 (e13cf15)``
## under node 24.11.1. The other five slices were generated by the same
## command and not executed. The gateway, channels, and the native
## add-ons were not exercised.
##
## ## Node
##
## ``engines.node`` is ``>=24.16.0 <25 || >=26.1.0``. The launcher resolves
## ``node`` from PATH, so a recipe using this package must declare a
## suitable node; the package cannot express that. It was run only under
## 24.11.1, which upstream warns is unsupported ("diagnostics may show
## truncated text").
##
## ``postinstall`` (``scripts/postinstall-bundled-plugins.mjs``: prune old
## ``dist`` files, repair a missing fs-safe addon) is an npm lifecycle step
## and does not run here. The addon it repairs is in the closure, and a
## fresh unpack has no stale ``dist`` to prune.
##
## ## Runtime facts
##
## * Credentials: model-provider API keys (for example ``ANTHROPIC_API_KEY``,
##   ``OPENAI_API_KEY``) or OAuth profiles stored under the state directory;
##   the gateway's shared secret is ``OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN`` or
##   ``OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PASSWORD`` (or ``gateway.auth.*`` in the config).
##   State and config live in ``~/.openclaw``; ``OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`` and
##   ``OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`` relocate them.
## * Network: the gateway listens on ``ws://127.0.0.1:18789`` (the control UI
##   is served there; ``OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PORT`` or ``--port`` changes it);
##   ``telemetry.openclaw.ai`` (``GET /api/latest-version``, the daily update
##   check, carrying version, OS, node version and CPU architecture); and
##   whichever model providers and chat platforms the user configures.
## * Self-update: on by default as a daily check, with automatic apply
##   configurable. Upstream's opt-outs are ``update.checkOnStart: false`` in
##   the config and ``OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1`` in the environment, which
##   also stops automatic applies. Each slice declares
##   ``env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1"``, exported by the ``tarball`` record as
##   a binding written by ``repro home apply`` as a persistent user environment variable (a managed block in the shell rc file on POSIX, the user registry on Windows)
##   (not a wrapper, and only home apply writes it: a process that does not
##   read that rc file, or a ``uses:`` dev environment, is not covered). ``update.checkOnStart``
##   is a config field the record kinds cannot set, so the daily check itself is
##   not disabled.
##   ``openclaw update`` remains an explicit user command that would try to
##   change an installed tree.
##
## ## Slices
##
## Six explicit slices, one per npm (os, cpu) pair upstream's optional
## dependencies cover for the desktop-class hosts: linux, macos and windows,
## each on x86_64 and aarch64. The root digest is the SAME for all six (it
## is one platform-independent tarball); what differs, and what the catalog
## test must check for distinctness, is the closure manifest, exactly as for
## ``amp``.

import repro_project_dsl

const
  OpenClawVersion = "2026.11.5"
  OpenClawSha256 =
    "a57d1272b7d87bdbf2b0a0e18811dc1ca3ffc5de02229d1f9e2884bd38470794"
  OpenClawUrl =
    "https://registry.npmjs.org/openclaw/-/openclaw-" & OpenClawVersion & ".tgz"

provisioningFor "openclaw":
  interfaceFingerprint "87cf417b168cc394cc691c71fd6cc9d6b6fefebe7b4ff5033b63b2134ecbbdeb"
  contributor "github:metacraft-labs/reprobuild-llm-agent-packages"

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-win32-x64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "x86_64",
    os = "windows",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":windows-x86_64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-win32-arm64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "aarch64",
    os = "windows",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":windows-aarch64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-darwin-arm64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "aarch64",
    os = "macos",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":macos-aarch64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-darwin-x64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "x86_64",
    os = "macos",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":macos-x86_64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-linux-x64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "x86_64",
    os = "linux",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":linux-x86_64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

  tarball url = OpenClawUrl,
    sha256 = OpenClawSha256,
    archiveType = "tar.gz",
    stripComponents = 1,
    executablePath = "openclaw.mjs",
    executableAlias = "openclaw",
    launcher = "node",
    closureManifest = "closures/openclaw-linux-arm64.manifest",
    env = "OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1",
    packageId = "openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion,
    cpu = "aarch64",
    os = "linux",
    lockIdentity = "vendor-npm:openclaw@" & OpenClawVersion &
      ":linux-aarch64:sha256:" & OpenClawSha256

# Every provider module of a catalog is extracted on its own by
# `repro catalog publish` and lifted into the artifact of ONE package, named
# by this block; the realizations above are the contributions it carries.
package openclawRealizations:
  discard
